Well, I finally got upgraded to 3.1 after years of playing 3.0.  I have a 
couple of questions/comments:

1) First of all, I really like it.  The line-of-sight is nice, the 
monsters with weapons is very nice (though very shocking the first time a 
monster attacks you with a wand) and the different dungeons are great.

2) What causes the increases/decreases in attributes (which is a nice 
touch I think).  I can understand that lifting things would make you 
stronger, but what causes decreases in dexterity? 

3) How can I change my dark blue so that it's a little lighter? I'm on an 
IBM PC and it's very tough to make out the dark blue nymphs against the 
black or grey background.

4) The town is really great too.  I like the touch of keeping some of the 
doors locked.  Trying to balance out my curiosity (what is in those 
rooms) with caution with a good character has been fun.

5) Do people generally find 3.1 easier than 3.0?  I'm one of those 
hopeless players who really enjoyes nethack, but has never won, although 
I've gotten pretty far down.  But the current version seems quite a bit 
easier for Valkyries.  I can see that Priests would have a field day with 
all the armour and weapons lying around.

